/*
 * walle_esp32.ino
 * WALL-E Smart Robot — ESP32-S3
 *
 * Modules:
 *   M1  — Audio Capture   (INMP441, I2S, VAD)
 *   M2  — Comms           (WiFi AP, HTTP client to Python)
 *   M3  — Command Parser  (JSON → RobotIntent)
 *   M4  — Action Dispatcher (state machine)
 *   M5  — Motion Controller (servos + motors)
 *   M6  — Expression Engine (TFT eyes)
 *   M7  — Web UI Server   (dashboard + manual trigger)
 *
 * Pin config: STRICTLY unchanged from test code.
 * Non-blocking: uses millis() everywhere, no delay() in main loop.
 * FreeRTOS: audio capture on Core 0, everything else on Core 1.
 *
 * Dependencies (install via Arduino Library Manager):
 *   - ESP32Servo
 *   - Adafruit GFX Library
 *   - Adafruit ST7735 and ST7789 Library
 *   - ArduinoJson  (v7)
 *   - HTTPClient   (built-in ESP32 core)
 */

